# Linear — mandatory (every session, every agent)

**Non-negotiable.** Applies to local Cursor, Cloud Agents, background agents, and subagents — not only feature implementation.

Linear is the **system of record** for approved issue scope, lifecycle state, and closure. GitHub PR linkbacks and bot comments **do not** replace agent-owned Linear updates when an approved Linear owner exists.

## Scope-mutation guardrail

Separate lifecycle/evidence maintenance from backlog-shape mutation.

Agents may directly update an **already-approved issue boundary** when evidence supports only lifecycle/evidence changes: implementation progress, PR/review links, truthful status movement, verified closure, or concise factual notes that do not expand scope.

Agents must **not** create a new issue, child, parent, contradiction issue, relationship, reparenting, or durable scope merely because work is discovered. New or changed scope must return to the Containment Protocol approval flow:

1. Phase 1 — candidate assessment and production decomposition;
2. Phase 2 — parent reconciliation and approval;
3. Phase 3 — child/supporting-work reconciliation, mandatory contradiction review, and approval;
4. Phase 4 — approved Linear update.

When approval state is absent or ambiguous, fail closed: preserve the finding as candidate/deferred evidence and do not mutate backlog shape.

## When to update

| Phase | Linear action |
| --- | --- |
| **Task start — approved implementation/harvest** | Use the already-approved slice/workflow issue named by the task and set it **In Progress** when substantive owned work begins. If feature scope has no approved owner, stop that scope and route it through candidate governance instead of creating one from this rule. |
| **Task start — unowned review/docs analysis** | A review, audit, or docs analysis that has no named approved Linear owner may proceed **read-only with no Linear mutation**. Do not manufacture an issue merely to satisfy this rule. If the work discovers durable product scope, record it as candidate input for the approval flow. |
| **During owned work** | Keep the approved slice current with material progress/blocker comments. Harvest triage follows `docs/harvest-candidate-triage-agent.md`; missing boundaries remain candidates until the approval flow reaches Phase 4. |
| **Slice ready** | **Commit**, **push**, and **open PR** on the named branch before claiming the approved slice complete locally (`implementation-lite.mdc` ship loop). |
| **PR opened** | Link the **slice** issue in the PR body (not only the parent epic); comment PR URL on the slice issue. |
| **Babysit → merge** | Same session: independent review + comment triage + CI until green, merge PR, then `git checkout main` && `git pull origin main` (`implementation-lite.mdc`). |
| **PR merged** | Set slice issue **Done** only when its full approved boundary is satisfied; parent **Done** only if full parent scope shipped, otherwise keep the truthful parent status. |
| **After merge** | Short comment on the slice issue: PR URL + what shipped + validation. |

## Do not skip because

- The PR has a GitHub linkback bot comment.
- An **owned** task was docs-only, harvest-only, or review-only.
- Linear MCP failed once; report the exact legal updates to apply and retry when possible.
- A prior agent already commented; add closure for **this** session's implementation evidence when relevant.

For an **unowned read-only review/docs session**, no Linear mutation is required or permitted solely for bookkeeping. “Linear mandatory” means respect existing Linear authority when one exists; it does not mean create authority when none exists.

## Cloud Agent → local-agent Linear handoff

Emit only after a Cloud Agent **implemented an already-approved plan to completion and merged** that implementation PR when Linear was not updated in-session. Planning-only PRs, open PRs, unowned read-only reviews/docs, and harvest sessions do not trigger it. Canonical: `docs/cloud-agent-linear-handoff.md`; tracked rule `.cursor/rules/cloud-agent-linear-handoff.mdc`.

## Authoritative detail

Full lifecycle, harvest batches, and documentation hygiene: `AGENTS.md` and `docs/agent-session-handoff.md`. If older repository wording implies autonomous scope creation, this approval-gated rule controls and the older wording must be treated as stale until corrected.
